# 숨은 이야기 「마중 나간 사람」 영어판
EN = {
"hidden_scylla_0": ("The Ships the Storm Followed",
 "Surveyor, I found something odd while tidying the ledgers. The Storm Survey Corps' ships. Seventeen have come from across the sea so far. Would you look at the arrival records side by side.",
 "Go through the arrival ledger with Haru the town clerk.",
 "Let me sum up. All seventeen came in under a storm. Not one exception. Yet no ship was wrecked. Not a sail torn. The crews say the same thing: 'the storm circled the ship once and passed.' …The Order gave the 'Storm Survey Corps' its name. I took it to mean you survey storms. Perhaps it meant the ships a storm surveys. Ledgers cannot lie."),
"hidden_scylla_kas_a": ("The Debtor Remembers",
 "A bundle came for you. Tied to an arrow, from the direction of the eastern tower. One line in charcoal on the outside: 'The debtor remembers.' It's Kas. The captain you let go. Let's open it together. …Honestly, I'm a little afraid.",
 "Open the bundle Kas sent together with Isabel the archivist.",
 "A scrap of banner. With the second verse of the song stitched on it. And between the folds a broken piece of a seal. Handed down in Kas's family, he says. 'What an ancestor who stepped off a ship was holding.' So not all of the Ashen Band descend from those left on land. Some stepped off ships. Which ships?"),
"hidden_scylla_kas_b": ("The Second Verse on the Wall",
 "Surveyor, come down under the Order with me. To Kas's cell. I brought his meal and it was empty. Still locked. I asked the Elder and he said only 'I let him go.' He wouldn't say why. There's something scratched on the wall. I'm afraid to read it alone.",
 "In the empty cell under the Order, examine what is left on the wall.",
 "It was the second verse of the song. Scratched with fingernails. And this piece of a seal under the cot. Left on purpose. The lowest line on the wall is for us. 'Your Elder listened to this song at the door every night. He wept at the second verse. Ask him why.' …I can't ask. Not yet."),
"hidden_scylla_1": ("The Lightning Has Eight Forks",
 "The clerk asked me about storms. The one that follows every Corps ship. I've cast nets in that sea all my life. Once, just once, I went into the middle of it. When I was young. I'll tell you. In return bring me a nautilus shell. They only came up in the net the day after that storm passed. Haven't caught one in years. The storm's been pinned in the north.",
 "Bring 1 nautilus shell to Oscar the fisherman and hear his story.",
 "Yes, this. Hold it to your ear. That's not waves. It's a tune. The tune I heard inside that storm. …I heard it the year the sea froze, too. The night before. Very near. From where Captain Cornelia's ship had gone. I never told anyone. I didn't know whether the storm followed the ship or the ship sailed into the storm."),
"hidden_scylla_2": ("The Log of the Welcome",
 "You have all five. The coin, the scale, the song, the log scrap, the seal. I laid them out on the desk and looked at them for three days. They aren't separate things. They all belonged to one person. They fell out of one logbook. Let's piece them together. You picked them up, so your eyes will see it first. And I don't think I'll want to be alone when I've read it.",
 "Fit the five clues together with Isabel the archivist.",
 "The eighth king had a twin sister. Admiral of the Isle of Dawn. She carried the king to the council by ship and promised to come out and welcome him when he returned. The day his name burned she was at sea, and she wrapped her fleet in a storm. Because the world cannot see inside the eye of a storm. So she was not forgotten. But she forgot whom she had come to meet. For a thousand years she has looked into every passing ship. Ours too. …Surveyor, she is no monster. She is keeping a promise."),
"hidden_scylla_3": ("Those Who Never Disembarked",
 "The archivist girl told me. That there have been people inside that storm for a thousand years. The ones I saw on that deck. …Let's find a wreck. Now and then a ship gets pushed out of the storm. Once it's outside the eye it eats a thousand years in a day. Rots and sinks. What's left aboard will tell us how they live in there. I'm coming. I know a little about waiting at sea.",
 "Find a shipwreck with Oscar and examine what is left in the cabin.",
 "Every rope was coiled. Ready to throw. Re-coiled every day for a thousand years. And that roster. The column for the day each sailor disembarked, empty all the way down. Not one went ashore. Nobody leaves until the admiral has finished her welcome. …Just like Captain Cornelia. Nobody dies on my ship. Nobody leaves this one. Captains."),
"hidden_scylla_4": ("Into the Eye of the Storm",
 "…Sit. Isabel came to me. With the five pieces. Laid them on my desk without a word. She did not ask. So I will tell. I know her. My master's… no. The old king's sister. You hold the storm eye? Then the storm will let you in. Go to the palace on the sea. And see there, for yourself, what I did.",
 "Carrying the storm eye, find the palace on the sea and examine the empty banquet hall.",
 "So you saw the table she keeps laid. …Yes. I sent it. Cornelia's ship. I wanted to hear whether, when she looked into a ship, she would speak the name of the one she sought. I told the captain to write it down. She did not speak a name. She does not know it. And in the middle of the storm a frightened sailor dropped anchor, and the anchor struck the seal. The sea froze. I burned a ship to hear one name. I have no excuse. Go and put her to rest. I cannot. She knows my face. She would ask me: 'Where is the boy?'"),
"hidden_scylla_5": ("The Storm Empress",
 "You're going? Then take this. My lamp. The one I put out the day my son came home. You don't tell someone who waits 'that's enough' with a sword. Still, there's no getting through that storm without one. She isn't bound to a seal but to a promise, the archivist says, so she can't be brought into a gate. You face her in the heart of the storm. The lightning has eight forks. Mind the eighth. That one she throws herself.",
 "In the palace on the sea, put Scylla the Storm Empress to rest. (Deal at least 10% of her health.)",
 "The storm lifted. I saw it all from the dock. Stars in the northern sky for the first time in a thousand years. And the ships came in. Ships with lightning on their sails. People stepped ashore. One by one. Each touched ground and looked back. For the admiral. …Go to the archivist. She's standing on the dock with the roster. Says she'll fill in the 'day disembarked'."),
"hidden_scylla_6": ("The Welcome",
 "You were on the dock. I was taking down the sailors' names. More than three hundred. Every one wrote today's date under 'day disembarked'. But the top line is left. The admiral's. She asked you at the end, they say. Where that person is. You know, don't you. Where the eighth king is. And that he chose it. What did you tell her?",
 "Tell Isabel the archivist what you answered the Storm Empress.",
 "I'll write it. On the top line. 'She Who Welcomes'. Admiral of the Isle of Dawn. Who laid a table for a thousand years after forgetting whom she had come to meet. Day disembarked… I'll leave it blank. She did not disembark. She went to meet him. Truly, this time. (Isabel closes the roster.) Surveyor. In the prologue they said our ship broke through a storm. It didn't. She looked at each face, and let us pass."),
}
